<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Udmurts</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Votyaks</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Udmurts are a Finno-Ugric people of the lands between the Vyatka and Kama rivers, most of whom live in the Udmurt Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, with its capital at Izhevsk. They came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and later the Khanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazan">Kazan</a>, and most were absorbed into Russia after the fall of Kazan in 1552. Their Permic language is closely related to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/komi-peoples">Komi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/udmurts.jpg" alt="Udmurts" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sirelius, U. T. · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Udmurts_1907.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
